1
00:00:04,733 --> 00:00:11,567
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:32,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:32,967 --> 00:00:34,033
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,733 --> 00:00:40,567
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:41,967 --> 00:00:43,033
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,167 --> 00:00:43,833
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:43,967 --> 00:00:45,300
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,633 --> 00:00:48,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,533 --> 00:00:51,467
[GUNSHOT]

10
00:00:52,233 --> 00:00:53,200
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:55,200
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:57,467
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:57,600 --> 00:00:59,033
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:02,567
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,300
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:06,933 --> 00:01:09,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:09,267 --> 00:01:11,333
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,467 --> 00:01:12,667
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:14,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:21,567
Sir, I heard things blew up here
<i> because of Mr. Chan.</i>

21
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:22,800
<i>They'll use all their money
and all their connections.</i>

22
00:01:22,933 --> 00:01:25,000
<i>They'll do everything to get
their son out of jail.</i>

23
00:01:25,133 --> 00:01:30,433
<i>Sam, focus on facing
the Internal Affairs.</i>

24
00:01:30,567 --> 00:01:32,633
<i>We'd like to visit the family
of the man who was shot</i>

25
00:01:32,767 --> 00:01:33,933
<i> during the demolition.</i>

26
00:01:34,067 --> 00:01:36,600
<i>Go ahead. I don't want to be
surprised if we fail again.</i>

27
00:01:36,733 --> 00:01:37,700
<i> Copy, sir.</i>

28
00:01:37,833 --> 00:01:38,833
- [SCREAMING]
- [GUNSHOT]

29
00:01:38,967 --> 00:01:39,800
<i> Ahh!</i>

30
00:01:39,933 --> 00:01:41,133
<i> Help!</i>

31
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:42,833
- [BLOWS LANDING]
<i> - Ma!</i>

32
00:01:42,967 --> 00:01:44,100
<i>- Ahh!
- Stop it, sir!</i>

33
00:01:44,233 --> 00:01:46,700
<i> Please help my mom!</i>

34
00:01:47,467 --> 00:01:48,333
<i> Help!</i>

35
00:01:48,467 --> 00:01:52,667
<i> Sir, will my mother survive?</i>

36
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,900
<i> Will she live?</i>

37
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:58,300
<i>I thought of a way
to find out Gabo's secret.</i>

38
00:01:58,433 --> 00:01:59,700
<i> I'll use Tolits and Binoy.</i>

39
00:01:59,833 --> 00:02:00,900
Can we ask what happened to him?

40
00:02:01,033 --> 00:02:02,433
<i>You sound like
you're not from here.</i>

41
00:02:02,567 --> 00:02:03,633
<i>This is one of Django's
gambling spots!</i>

42
00:02:03,767 --> 00:02:04,633
<i> Come on, let's go.</i>

43
00:02:06,267 --> 00:02:07,333
- Aah!
- Django!

44
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,600
Surprise!

45
00:02:08,733 --> 00:02:10,133
- It's Django!
- Get them!

46
00:02:10,267 --> 00:02:12,833
- Make way!
- Run, hurry!

47
00:02:12,967 --> 00:02:15,633
- [THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]
- [ROOSTER CROWING IN DISTANCE]

48
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:16,700
Move!

49
00:02:17,133 --> 00:02:19,200
[SCREAMING]

50
00:02:19,333 --> 00:02:21,567
Out of my way!
I'm in a hurry!

51
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:28,033
- [GRUNTS]
- [LOUD THUD]

52
00:02:28,167 --> 00:02:29,733
- Hey!
- Oh no!

53
00:02:29,867 --> 00:02:32,100
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

54
00:02:32,233 --> 00:02:33,367
I'm being chased!

55
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:34,600
Help!

56
00:02:34,733 --> 00:02:35,767
- Help!
- Hey!

57
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:36,200
Somebody, help!

58
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,233
[PANTING]

59
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:42,033
[THWACKS]

60
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,100
Move!

61
00:02:43,233 --> 00:02:45,000
Help! Please help!

62
00:02:45,133 --> 00:02:47,733
- They're coming!
- Keep running!

63
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:48,933
[PANICKED BREATHS]

64
00:02:49,067 --> 00:02:50,400
[OVERLAPPING SHOUTING]

65
00:02:50,533 --> 00:02:51,267
This way!

66
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:52,967
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

67
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:55,400
- [TOLITS] You win! Enough!
- [BINOY PANTING]

68
00:02:55,533 --> 00:02:57,233
- Django! Django!
- [DABOY] We give up!

69
00:02:57,367 --> 00:02:59,967
- Django, don't hurt us!
- [BINOY] Have mercy!

70
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:00,933
[DOG BARKING IN DISTANCE]

71
00:03:01,067 --> 00:03:03,467
Stand up.
I just want to talk.

72
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:04,700
Huh?

73
00:03:05,267 --> 00:03:06,533
Why did you chase us
if you just wanted to talk?

74
00:03:06,667 --> 00:03:08,233
Well, you started running!
Now, get up!

75
00:03:08,367 --> 00:03:10,033
What do you want
from us, Django?

76
00:03:10,167 --> 00:03:11,667
[DJANGO MOCKING]

77
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:12,667
No!

78
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:14,800
I just want to ask you
a question.

79
00:03:15,167 --> 00:03:16,233
Come with us.

80
00:03:16,233 --> 00:03:17,800
Django, I don't like your face!

81
00:03:17,933 --> 00:03:20,167
- We're going nowhere, Django!
- Look, we're fine here.

82
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:21,967
- Thanks, but no thanks.
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

83
00:03:22,133 --> 00:03:23,133
- [GUN COCKS]
- We're coming.

84
00:03:23,267 --> 00:03:25,600
So where to, Django?
I like hanging out with you.

85
00:03:26,067 --> 00:03:27,367
[BINOY] Let's go.

86
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:30,067
- We'll go anywhere--
- You had us chasing you!

87
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:32,300
- Move your feet!
- How's my godchild?

88
00:03:32,433 --> 00:03:33,400
See the irony?

89
00:03:33,667 --> 00:03:37,433
You were furious when I hired
Betchay to work in BeerGin.

90
00:03:38,033 --> 00:03:40,500
Now, she's of use to us.

91
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:45,400
We learned from her
that Gabo received

92
00:03:45,533 --> 00:03:48,533
200,000 pesos.

93
00:03:48,667 --> 00:03:51,400
You know,
that detail doesn't matter

94
00:03:51,533 --> 00:03:54,067
if we don't know
where the money came from.

95
00:03:54,233 --> 00:03:55,833
Exactly, Ibyang!

96
00:03:55,967 --> 00:03:56,967
Django is working on it.

97
00:03:57,100 --> 00:03:59,433
For your information,

98
00:03:59,567 --> 00:04:01,900
even without
the help of Betchay,

99
00:04:02,033 --> 00:04:03,700
we would be able
to figure it out.

100
00:04:03,833 --> 00:04:05,100
Gossip travels fast around here.

101
00:04:05,233 --> 00:04:08,433
Still, it's different
when information comes

102
00:04:08,567 --> 00:04:10,967
from someone close to Gabo.

103
00:04:11,333 --> 00:04:12,233
- Just focus on your food.
- [GLASS THUDS]

104
00:04:13,933 --> 00:04:14,933
Hey, it's confirmed.

105
00:04:14,933 --> 00:04:17,267
That's why they had
a fight last night.

106
00:04:17,333 --> 00:04:19,867
[WOMAN] Is Betchay really
that desperate...

107
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,733
- I guess.
- ...to work in BeerGin?

108
00:04:21,733 --> 00:04:23,867
Hey, Ma!
Miss Betchay might hear you!

109
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:25,567
You'll get into trouble again!

110
00:04:25,567 --> 00:04:27,033
Shut that mouth of yours!

111
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,433
That's what gets you in trouble!

112
00:04:28,567 --> 00:04:29,533
[DIDAY] But it's true!

113
00:04:30,133 --> 00:04:31,667
Once a woman is dirty,
she's nothing but dirty!

114
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:33,700
- [WOMAN] Exactly!
- Dirty?!

115
00:04:33,833 --> 00:04:34,733
- [ESTONG] Ma...
- Who's dirty?

116
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:37,133
- You're the dirty one!
- Listen to me!

117
00:04:37,267 --> 00:04:38,667
- I'll tell you who's dirty!
- What do you want?

118
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:40,333
- This is your fault, Ma!
- You and your mouth!

119
00:04:40,333 --> 00:04:44,067
So get a scrub and scrape
that filthy mouth!

120
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,767
I'm sorry, Miss Betchay.

121
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:47,700
You better put a muzzle
on your mother!

122
00:04:47,833 --> 00:04:48,967
- She keeps barking!
- What, like a dog?!

123
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:50,367
- Bingo!
- Really now?!

124
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:51,367
- Think I'm scared of you?
- I'm just speaking facts!

125
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:53,833
Don't try me, Diday!
I'll stand my ground!

126
00:04:53,967 --> 00:04:55,100
- I won't back down!
- Ouch!

127
00:04:55,233 --> 00:04:57,500
Now, quit acting
like you're all clean!

128
00:04:57,633 --> 00:05:00,967
Because we're all dirty,
anyway!

129
00:05:01,133 --> 00:05:02,533
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

130
00:05:02,667 --> 00:05:04,867
- You're working in BeerGin!
- You'd think you were saints...

131
00:05:06,833 --> 00:05:08,033
Ma'am.

132
00:05:08,167 --> 00:05:10,267
Do you think the Magtibays
will actually talk to us?

133
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:12,933
They might just throw us
out again,

134
00:05:13,067 --> 00:05:14,100
especially the son.

135
00:05:14,233 --> 00:05:16,733
We've got nothing to lose
if we try.

136
00:05:18,300 --> 00:05:18,867
- [BETCHAY] Miss Beautiful!
- Oh.

137
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,233
Coming to our house again?

138
00:05:21,367 --> 00:05:24,167
Yes. We just wanted to check in.

139
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:26,700
Is Mister Rudy doing better now?

140
00:05:26,833 --> 00:05:29,100
Yes, he's out of the hospital.

141
00:05:29,233 --> 00:05:30,667
[INHALES DEEPLY]

142
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:33,433
The hospital bill was insane.

143
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:36,233
We even went into debt.

144
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:38,800
The money you gave hardly
made a difference.

145
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:41,167
[ESTRELLA] Oh, dear.

146
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:44,400
Good thing we came by.

147
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:45,833
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

148
00:05:45,833 --> 00:05:47,500
We actually wanted
to talk to your husband

149
00:05:47,633 --> 00:05:48,533
about what happened.

150
00:05:48,667 --> 00:05:49,167
[SILLY MUSIC PLAYING]

151
00:05:50,133 --> 00:05:51,667
To settle things?

152
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:52,933
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

153
00:05:52,933 --> 00:05:53,867
Yes.

154
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:54,567
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

155
00:05:55,967 --> 00:06:00,567
[MEN CHATTING INDISTINCTLY]

156
00:06:00,567 --> 00:06:01,900
- Mister Rudy!
- It's really him!

157
00:06:02,033 --> 00:06:03,467
- Look, it's Rudy!
- Where are you going?

158
00:06:04,033 --> 00:06:05,500
Just going to get
some medicine.

159
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:06,367
Ah.

160
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:08,133
Mister Rudy, would you like
to make a bet?

161
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:09,933
- Yeah, join us!
- Especially since...

162
00:06:10,067 --> 00:06:12,133
You've almost died.

163
00:06:12,267 --> 00:06:13,767
- [MEN] Oh, yeah.
- They say that's lucky.

164
00:06:13,900 --> 00:06:15,367
- Yes, come on!
- You might have luck, Rudy.

165
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:16,767
- Come on!
- Come on!

166
00:06:16,900 --> 00:06:18,400
Don't think twice. Come on over.

167
00:06:18,533 --> 00:06:20,600
Don't keep your luck waiting.
Come on!

168
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:22,933
We'll double your money.
I can guarantee that.

169
00:06:23,067 --> 00:06:24,900
- Go on, drag him here.
- Come on!

170
00:06:25,033 --> 00:06:26,933
- Come on, Rudy.
- Join us, Rudy.

171
00:06:27,067 --> 00:06:28,200
We need one more player.

172
00:06:28,333 --> 00:06:30,000
Don't play hard to get!
Get over here!

173
00:06:30,133 --> 00:06:32,000
- Hurry, Rudy.
- This'll be quick.

174
00:06:32,133 --> 00:06:33,633
Come on, let's start.

175
00:06:33,767 --> 00:06:35,333
We'll be here no matter
how many rounds it takes.

176
00:06:35,467 --> 00:06:36,867
- You can do better than that.
- Fine.

177
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,667
- Game?
- Where's your bet?

178
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:40,633
- All in?
- Sure.

179
00:06:44,867 --> 00:06:46,133
You know what...
[CLEARS THROAT]

180
00:06:46,267 --> 00:06:47,000
I'll be honest with you.

181
00:06:47,133 --> 00:06:50,733
I know you're not from an NGO.

182
00:06:50,867 --> 00:06:55,633
Or maybe you're even
with the cops who came here.

183
00:06:55,767 --> 00:06:57,933
- Is that right, miss?
- [MAX CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

184
00:06:58,067 --> 00:06:59,133
- Am I right?
- Of course not.

185
00:06:59,267 --> 00:07:01,033
We're really from a
non-governmental organization.

186
00:07:01,167 --> 00:07:02,100
- You sure?
- Of course.

187
00:07:02,233 --> 00:07:03,200
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

188
00:07:03,333 --> 00:07:04,967
All we really want
is peace and order.

189
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:08,633
We can wrap this up

190
00:07:08,767 --> 00:07:11,333
if you can take us
to where your husband is.

191
00:07:11,467 --> 00:07:14,167
- We're easy to talk to.
- Yes, we really are.

192
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:16,467
I don't think it's a good time.

193
00:07:16,633 --> 00:07:17,600
He's not in a good mood.

194
00:07:17,733 --> 00:07:20,900
And then you'll talk to him
about what happened?

195
00:07:21,033 --> 00:07:23,067
I thinks it's a bad time.

196
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:25,200
- Ahh.
- Oh, is that so, ma'am?

197
00:07:25,333 --> 00:07:26,800
If that is the case,

198
00:07:26,933 --> 00:07:28,733
when is a better time
to come back?

199
00:07:28,867 --> 00:07:30,067
How about this,

200
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:33,200
just tell me
what you want from him.

201
00:07:33,333 --> 00:07:36,733
Then I'll talk to Rudy
and her sister.

202
00:07:36,867 --> 00:07:38,700
And when he's decided,

203
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:40,433
his son wouldn't be able
to do anything about it.

204
00:07:40,567 --> 00:07:41,467
- Ahh.
- Hmm.

205
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:42,033
Here.

206
00:07:42,167 --> 00:07:44,033
Give me your number

207
00:07:44,167 --> 00:07:47,333
so we can talk over the phone.

208
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:48,933
It's a bit of a hassle
going back here.

209
00:07:49,067 --> 00:07:50,033
Sure, ma'am.

210
00:07:50,167 --> 00:07:51,100
Here.

211
00:07:51,233 --> 00:07:54,967
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

212
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:56,133
Aren't you forgetting something?

213
00:07:56,267 --> 00:07:58,967
You know, it'll be easier
to talk to Rudy

214
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:03,733
if I tell him I paid off
some of our debts.

215
00:08:03,867 --> 00:08:05,067
- Because--
- Here you go.

216
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:08,100
I'm sorry it slipped our minds.

217
00:08:08,233 --> 00:08:09,333
[ALL CHUCKLING]

218
00:08:09,467 --> 00:08:11,133
Thank you! Oh, you're too kind!

219
00:08:11,267 --> 00:08:14,900
Oh, he actually
has a sister, Mameng.

220
00:08:15,033 --> 00:08:17,167
Oh, I'll tell you
she's a tough cookie.

221
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:19,533
And she's really close
with Rudy.

222
00:08:19,667 --> 00:08:22,467
And we need to
have her on board too, right?

223
00:08:22,633 --> 00:08:24,533
- What do we do?
- If that's the case, ma'am...

224
00:08:24,667 --> 00:08:27,100
- uh, here.
- [QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

225
00:08:27,233 --> 00:08:28,167
Please accept it.

226
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:30,033
Do you have any more relatives?

227
00:08:30,167 --> 00:08:32,133
That's about it.

228
00:08:32,267 --> 00:08:35,533
I'll talk to them.
Don't worry.

229
00:08:35,667 --> 00:08:39,033
I'll do everything I can
to convince them,

230
00:08:39,167 --> 00:08:40,867
and believe me,
we'll have this settled.

231
00:08:40,867 --> 00:08:45,533
You'll get their sweet yeses.

232
00:08:45,667 --> 00:08:46,800
[SMACK]

233
00:08:46,933 --> 00:08:48,767
I'll get going.
You should get home.

234
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:49,733
[MAX CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

235
00:08:49,867 --> 00:08:52,800
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

236
00:08:52,933 --> 00:08:54,200
Just wow.

237
00:08:54,367 --> 00:08:58,000
Ma'am, that lady
just wanted money.

238
00:08:58,133 --> 00:09:02,067
We can use up all of
NLEA's funds for this,

239
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:03,400
but still nothing could happen.

240
00:09:03,533 --> 00:09:07,100
Just one of them disagrees,
and we're doomed.

241
00:09:07,233 --> 00:09:09,000
We won't be able to settle this.

242
00:09:09,133 --> 00:09:10,500
The case might still
push through.

243
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:12,200
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

244
00:09:12,333 --> 00:09:14,967
I think the dad will take
the bribe we'll throw at him.

245
00:09:16,933 --> 00:09:18,833
The son, on the other hand...

246
00:09:19,933 --> 00:09:22,500
we'll figure out
how to make him cave.

247
00:09:24,933 --> 00:09:27,167
Uh, ma'am, ma'am.

248
00:09:27,167 --> 00:09:28,833
Patient Linda Reyes.

249
00:09:28,867 --> 00:09:29,833
- Linda Reyes?
- Yes.

250
00:09:29,967 --> 00:09:31,767
She needs surgery.

251
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:33,233
They're preparing her right now.

252
00:09:33,367 --> 00:09:35,033
The surgery
needs a down payment.

253
00:09:35,167 --> 00:09:39,200
Uh, did you see a little boy?

254
00:09:39,867 --> 00:09:41,400
- [GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]
- Thank you so much.

255
00:09:41,533 --> 00:09:43,200
What's your name?

256
00:09:43,333 --> 00:09:44,200
Gabo.

257
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:46,300
Call me Gabo.

258
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:51,533
[NURSE] There he is.

259
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,233
Oh, Pochoy!

260
00:09:54,367 --> 00:09:54,867
- Auntie Mercy!
- Pochoy!

261
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:58,800
[BOTH SOBBING]

262
00:09:58,933 --> 00:10:02,500
Pochoy, I'm glad you're safe.

263
00:10:03,433 --> 00:10:04,000
What happened to your Mama?

264
00:10:04,133 --> 00:10:06,767
[CRYING] Auntie Mercy,

265
00:10:06,900 --> 00:10:08,867
Mama got shot!

266
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:13,533
Don't worry.
I know she'll be safe.

267
00:10:13,667 --> 00:10:17,733
[BOTH CRYING, SNIFFLING]

268
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:19,100
Uh, who are you?

269
00:10:22,733 --> 00:10:24,200
Uh...

270
00:10:24,333 --> 00:10:26,967
I helped Pochoy and his mom.

271
00:10:27,100 --> 00:10:29,867
I helped bring his mom here.

272
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,200
Thank you.

273
00:10:31,333 --> 00:10:34,000
I'm her mom's sister-in-law.

274
00:10:34,133 --> 00:10:38,333
Uh, thanks again
for taking her to the hospital.

275
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:40,933
I'll call your Papa,
okay, Pochoy?

276
00:10:41,067 --> 00:10:42,833
I'll just call his dad.

277
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:47,967
H-Hello? Hello, Mando.

278
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:51,933
Something bad happened to Linda.

279
00:10:52,067 --> 00:10:55,233
Uh, Pochoy and I are
in the hospital.

280
00:10:57,833 --> 00:10:59,933
S-She got shot.

281
00:11:00,067 --> 00:11:01,933
They got mugged.

282
00:11:02,067 --> 00:11:06,867
But Pochoy's here. He's safe.

283
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,200
What?

284
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:11,433
We really need the money.
[SNIFFLES]

285
00:11:12,367 --> 00:11:15,433
I'll wait for your call.
Okay, okay.

286
00:11:17,900 --> 00:11:18,833
[SIGHS]

287
00:11:18,967 --> 00:11:22,067
Auntie, what did Papa say?

288
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:26,367
Dear, your Papa doesn't have
the money yet.

289
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:28,967
He just asked for an advance
to pay for your tuition.

290
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:30,767
[SNIFFLES]

291
00:11:30,900 --> 00:11:31,867
Uh...

292
00:11:32,933 --> 00:11:33,333
Pochoy.

293
00:11:35,167 --> 00:11:36,600
Don't worry.

294
00:11:36,733 --> 00:11:40,433
I'll find a way so your mom
can get surgery.

295
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:43,333
Thank you, Gabo.

296
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:48,267
Mister, you don't even know us,
and we're not your family.

297
00:11:48,967 --> 00:11:51,733
But are you really
going to help us?

298
00:11:55,433 --> 00:11:56,767
[SOBBING]

299
00:11:56,767 --> 00:11:58,367
You're so kind.

300
00:11:59,567 --> 00:12:01,933
Thank you. Thank you.

301
00:12:02,067 --> 00:12:04,500
You're heaven-sent.

302
00:12:04,633 --> 00:12:05,900
Thank you!

303
00:12:06,033 --> 00:12:08,167
Pochoy, this kind man
is going to help us.

304
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:11,400
Pochoy.

305
00:12:12,433 --> 00:12:13,667
Don't worry.

306
00:12:14,867 --> 00:12:18,233
I'll find a way
so your mom can get surgery.

307
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:23,400
Thank you so much, Gabo.

308
00:12:23,533 --> 00:12:30,400
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

309
00:12:34,167 --> 00:12:35,167
Come on.

310
00:12:35,167 --> 00:12:38,267
Okay. Three, two, one, action.
Go.

311
00:12:38,267 --> 00:12:40,467
We are currently at
San Bernardino Hospital

312
00:12:40,467 --> 00:12:41,833
where a woman
who was robbed and shot

313
00:12:41,833 --> 00:12:43,167
has been admitted.

314
00:12:43,167 --> 00:12:44,200
Let's go inside.

315
00:12:46,167 --> 00:12:47,600
Stay here, okay?

316
00:12:48,533 --> 00:12:49,900
I'll be right back.

317
00:12:50,567 --> 00:12:53,367
I will find a way
to pay for your mom's operation.

318
00:12:53,367 --> 00:12:54,367
Alright.

319
00:12:54,367 --> 00:12:55,733
- Thank you.
- I'll be right back.

320
00:12:55,733 --> 00:12:56,900
Thank you again.

321
00:13:00,833 --> 00:13:04,233
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

322
00:13:04,233 --> 00:13:05,233
Gabo?

323
00:13:06,267 --> 00:13:07,733
What are you doing here?

324
00:13:07,733 --> 00:13:08,800
Ah...

325
00:13:10,233 --> 00:13:12,633
I brought the lady
who was robbed here.

326
00:13:13,533 --> 00:13:14,600
I helped her.

327
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:15,600
You helped another person?

328
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:19,533
First, it was me,
now that woman?

329
00:13:19,533 --> 00:13:21,700
Where is she?
We want to talk to her.

330
00:13:21,733 --> 00:13:23,367
She's in the operating room.

331
00:13:23,367 --> 00:13:25,633
But they can't proceed
until we settle the bill.

332
00:13:25,633 --> 00:13:27,733
I'm going to try to get
the money we need.

333
00:13:27,733 --> 00:13:29,133
Okay. We'll talk to her.

334
00:13:29,133 --> 00:13:31,033
But we'll interview you first.

335
00:13:31,033 --> 00:13:32,300
- Okay, okay.
- Go ahead.

336
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:36,867
That won't be necessary.

337
00:13:36,867 --> 00:13:38,700
Gabo, we need this interview.

338
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:40,667
You'll go viral for this!

339
00:13:40,667 --> 00:13:42,100
I don't care about that.

340
00:13:42,100 --> 00:13:44,867
You should talk to
the victim's family.

341
00:13:45,967 --> 00:13:47,367
Alright, I'm leaving.

342
00:13:49,267 --> 00:13:50,767
Who the hell is that?

343
00:13:50,767 --> 00:13:51,967
What a prick!

344
00:13:51,967 --> 00:13:52,967
Don't mind him.

345
00:13:52,967 --> 00:13:54,067
I'll tell you about it later.

346
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:58,000
Let's try her.

347
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,133
- Ma'am?
- [WOMAN WHIMPERS]

348
00:14:00,133 --> 00:14:01,800
Good day.

349
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:05,900
- Yes?
- Do you know the victim?

350
00:14:05,900 --> 00:14:07,600
Yes. Can I help you?

351
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:09,000
How do you know her?

352
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,100
She's my sister-in-law.

353
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:14,800
Did you witness the crime?

354
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:15,900
No, sir.

355
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:18,833
H-Her son was with her.

356
00:14:18,833 --> 00:14:21,433
May we speak with him?

357
00:14:21,433 --> 00:14:23,300
I don't think so.

358
00:14:23,300 --> 00:14:24,933
He's been through enough.

359
00:14:24,933 --> 00:14:28,000
Are you Salvador
"The Vindicator"?

360
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,700
- Yes, ma'am.
- Uh...

361
00:14:30,733 --> 00:14:33,033
You could interview me.

362
00:14:33,033 --> 00:14:35,167
- Oh, great.
- Alright, alright.

363
00:14:35,167 --> 00:14:36,700
- Stand here.
- Here, ma'am.

364
00:14:36,700 --> 00:14:38,467
Look this way, okay?

365
00:14:38,467 --> 00:14:40,867
- Straight to the camera.
- Wait. Hold on.

366
00:14:42,100 --> 00:14:45,300
Okay. Three, two, one, go.

367
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:49,167
Ma'am, can you tell us
what happened?

368
00:14:49,167 --> 00:14:51,767
My sister-in-law and her son
were going to enroll in school.

369
00:14:51,767 --> 00:14:57,067
Her husband, who works abroad,
just sent the money.

370
00:14:57,067 --> 00:15:01,133
But they were robbed.

371
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:06,800
My sister-in-law refused
to give the money.

372
00:15:06,800 --> 00:15:09,300
So they shot her.

373
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:13,300
How is she doing now, ma'am?

374
00:15:13,300 --> 00:15:14,400
Well... [SNIFFLES]

375
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:17,867
She has to undergo
an operation.

376
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:24,333
Good thing a man helped us...

377
00:15:24,333 --> 00:15:26,800
bring her to the hospital.

378
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:30,800
If not for him,
she wouldn't have made it.

379
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:36,700
H-He even promised to help
with the cost of the surgery.

380
00:15:36,733 --> 00:15:41,867
We are truly grateful
to this man. [SNIFFLES]

381
00:15:41,867 --> 00:15:44,033
Thank you, stranger.

382
00:15:45,567 --> 00:15:47,200
[ISOBEL]
Here. You can have these.

383
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:49,267
[TWINKLE]
Huh? Really, ma'am?

384
00:15:49,267 --> 00:15:52,300
Toto and I can use
your spa coupons?

385
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:56,400
I can't have either of you
come with me, can I?

386
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:58,000
Gee, ma'am!

387
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,367
Why don't you bring
Sir Ricardo with you?

388
00:16:00,367 --> 00:16:02,400
You two would have
a great time together.

389
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:04,100
Oh, please!

390
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:05,000
I don't want to.

391
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,867
I won't be able
to relax with him.

392
00:16:06,867 --> 00:16:08,967
- Oh, okay.
- Sir Ricardo's here!

393
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,800
- Huh?
- S-Sir!

394
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:13,133
Do you want to go to a spa
with Ma'am Isobel?

395
00:16:13,133 --> 00:16:14,533
- What?
- Shh!

396
00:16:14,533 --> 00:16:17,500
Ma'am Isobel was going
to bring Miss Sam with her.

397
00:16:17,500 --> 00:16:19,100
But Miss Sam's not available.

398
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:20,433
Leave him alone.

399
00:16:20,433 --> 00:16:21,567
Where is she?

400
00:16:22,667 --> 00:16:24,200
At the office.

401
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:28,600
Waiting to see
if she's getting fired.

402
00:16:30,433 --> 00:16:32,467
You didn't even ask about it?

403
00:16:34,267 --> 00:16:37,733
And what makes you think
I care about her career?

404
00:16:37,733 --> 00:16:43,833
To be honest, I don't know
what you care about anymore.

405
00:16:47,267 --> 00:16:49,400
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

406
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:50,333
Ma'am.

407
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:54,467
Oh-- [SHUSHES]
Come on.

408
00:16:55,167 --> 00:16:56,467
Hurry up.

409
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:06,533
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

410
00:17:12,267 --> 00:17:14,267
Good day, sir.

411
00:17:15,033 --> 00:17:17,033
Agent Jacinto.

412
00:17:17,033 --> 00:17:18,167
You may sit down.

413
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:28,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

414
00:17:28,133 --> 00:17:29,633
Agent Jacinto,

415
00:17:29,633 --> 00:17:30,567
the records clearly state

416
00:17:30,567 --> 00:17:32,433
that you made
an unauthorized arrest,

417
00:17:32,433 --> 00:17:34,633
conducted an interrogation
without clearance,

418
00:17:34,633 --> 00:17:38,967
and used force against a person
under NCIA custody.

419
00:17:38,967 --> 00:17:40,467
Is there anything
you want to say?

420
00:17:40,467 --> 00:17:43,533
I had no intention
of breaking the law, sir.

421
00:17:43,533 --> 00:17:46,567
All I wanted was
to catch Mr. Chan.

422
00:17:46,567 --> 00:17:49,233
Perhaps my methods were wrong.

423
00:17:49,267 --> 00:17:51,667
I even got the team involved.

424
00:17:51,667 --> 00:17:53,200
I won't deny that.

425
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:55,067
That was wrong.

426
00:17:55,067 --> 00:17:57,100
But if you were to ask me

427
00:17:57,100 --> 00:18:01,467
if I regret apprehending
Mr. Chan,

428
00:18:01,467 --> 00:18:02,800
absolutely not.

429
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:05,500
But the end does not
justify the means.

430
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:08,400
If law enforcement
is the first to break protocol

431
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:10,367
and disrespect the process,

432
00:18:10,367 --> 00:18:12,167
what can people expect of us?

433
00:18:12,167 --> 00:18:16,500
That we can solve a case
that others have given up on.

434
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:18,000
You know, you're lucky.

435
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:19,567
Because you caught him

436
00:18:19,567 --> 00:18:22,267
despite the violations
you committed.

437
00:18:22,300 --> 00:18:25,767
Mr. Chan's testimony
will determine your fate.

438
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:30,700
Agent Jacinto,

439
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:33,000
Internal Affairs will
deliberate on the evidence

440
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,500
and give their recommendations.

441
00:18:35,933 --> 00:18:38,467
Regardless of our decision,

442
00:18:38,467 --> 00:18:40,900
you may submit an appeal.

443
00:18:42,467 --> 00:18:44,533
Thank you for
giving me the opportunity

444
00:18:44,533 --> 00:18:46,567
to explain myself.

445
00:18:46,567 --> 00:18:48,467
Thank you also for your time.

446
00:18:48,467 --> 00:18:49,767
You may go.

447
00:18:49,767 --> 00:18:56,700
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

448
00:19:09,467 --> 00:19:11,333
[NARRATOR]<i> Crime in the country
</i> has continued to rise

449
00:19:11,467 --> 00:19:13,033
<i> because of poverty.</i>

450
00:19:13,167 --> 00:19:15,100
<i> - Hundreds of lives...
</i>- Pops.

451
00:19:15,233 --> 00:19:17,167
Our country is deteriorating.

452
00:19:17,300 --> 00:19:19,733
[OMENG] Unemployment rate
is on the rise.

453
00:19:19,733 --> 00:19:20,600
Crime is going rampant.

454
00:19:21,167 --> 00:19:23,733
People kill each other
out of poverty.

455
00:19:23,867 --> 00:19:25,533
The criminals
are getting braver.

456
00:19:25,667 --> 00:19:28,033
[TOMAS] They have no respect
for human life.

457
00:19:28,300 --> 00:19:29,767
They fear nothing.

458
00:19:29,900 --> 00:19:31,733
[NARRATOR]<i> ...to listen
</i> to the public's plea.

459
00:19:31,867 --> 00:19:36,033
And the people behind
this disorder...

460
00:19:36,433 --> 00:19:37,600
are the ones benefiting.

461
00:19:37,733 --> 00:19:40,300
We need to take them down.

462
00:19:40,433 --> 00:19:43,233
We're talking about
huge people here, Pops.

463
00:19:43,367 --> 00:19:44,533
We're not ready yet.

464
00:19:44,667 --> 00:19:47,733
And we can't just rush it, Pops.

465
00:19:47,867 --> 00:19:51,000
That's why we need to prepare.

466
00:19:51,133 --> 00:19:54,667
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

467
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:58,567
[PAPANG]<i> This country
</i> is riddled with chaos.

468
00:19:59,067 --> 00:20:03,300
<i>Unless we capture the people
behind all of this mess,</i>

469
00:20:04,100 --> 00:20:07,933
<i>Filipinos will remain
in the grip of the storm.</i>

470
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:13,233
<i>We need someone
to finally turn the tide.</i>

471
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:17,367
- On your knees.
- Huh?

472
00:20:17,500 --> 00:20:18,567
- Down!
- On your knees!

473
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:20,367
- Yeah, yeah!
- We're doing it!

474
00:20:20,500 --> 00:20:22,833
I thought he was talking
to you guys.

475
00:20:23,433 --> 00:20:25,067
[TOLITS] Uh...

476
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,967
Django, what do you
want from us?

477
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:30,200
Why did you bring us here?

478
00:20:30,333 --> 00:20:31,800
Please let us go.

479
00:20:31,933 --> 00:20:35,800
I told you.
I just want to talk.

480
00:20:36,733 --> 00:20:37,733
I just wanted
to ask you something.

481
00:20:39,567 --> 00:20:41,733
Where did Gabo get
that huge sum of money from?

482
00:20:43,533 --> 00:20:45,067
- Gabo has money?
- Huh?

483
00:20:45,467 --> 00:20:46,833
Where from?

484
00:20:46,967 --> 00:20:48,067
How huge is it?

485
00:20:48,200 --> 00:20:49,200
You really don't know?

486
00:20:49,333 --> 00:20:51,800
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

487
00:20:51,933 --> 00:20:52,933
[CHUCKLES]

488
00:20:53,733 --> 00:20:55,300
- [ALL SCREAM IN PANIC]
- [GUN COCKS]

489
00:20:55,433 --> 00:20:57,133
- Wait a minute--
- [SCREAMS]

490
00:20:57,267 --> 00:20:59,933
[TOLITS] Mama! Help me, Mama!

491
00:21:02,033 --> 00:21:02,967
How much?

492
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,333
How much for you to tell me
what Gabo is up to?

493
00:21:09,700 --> 00:21:11,400
Where did he get the 200,000?

494
00:21:12,533 --> 00:21:19,567
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

495
00:21:21,467 --> 00:21:22,367
[IN UNISON]
We don't know anything!

496
00:21:23,300 --> 00:21:24,233
Really? [CHUCKLES]

497
00:21:24,367 --> 00:21:25,633
- [ALL LAUGH]
- Not at all.

498
00:21:25,767 --> 00:21:27,033
- We have no idea.
- Nothing at all.

499
00:21:27,167 --> 00:21:28,533
[LAUGHING] No, nothing.

500
00:21:28,667 --> 00:21:30,100
It's impossible, right?
[LAUGHS PHONILY]

501
00:21:30,233 --> 00:21:31,133
Can we go now?

502
00:21:31,267 --> 00:21:32,400
That's not what I'm asking!

503
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:36,367
Are you rejecting
my money now?!

504
00:21:41,267 --> 00:21:44,967
Does Pops really want
to cleanse the country?

505
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,933
And are we supposed to do that?

506
00:21:46,933 --> 00:21:49,300
Ordinary Filipinos don't depend
on anyone else

507
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:51,033
aside from us.

508
00:21:51,167 --> 00:21:54,867
But Pops doesn't need
to take all responsibility.

509
00:21:55,267 --> 00:21:58,467
We all know why Pops
wants to do it.

510
00:21:58,600 --> 00:22:01,667
He was once
in that same situation.

511
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:02,567
But we're not ready.

512
00:22:02,700 --> 00:22:05,333
Who does he expect
to do all of this?

513
00:22:05,467 --> 00:22:07,533
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

514
00:22:07,667 --> 00:22:09,000
Oh, oh, oh.

515
00:22:09,967 --> 00:22:11,500
Don't tell me he meant Gabo.

516
00:22:11,867 --> 00:22:13,800
We're dealing
with prominent people.

517
00:22:13,933 --> 00:22:16,667
Gabo is helpless,
even with nine lives.

518
00:22:17,400 --> 00:22:20,667
He can't just attack them
like he always does.

519
00:22:20,967 --> 00:22:22,133
Uwak.

520
00:22:22,267 --> 00:22:24,367
That's exactly why we need
to be prepared.

521
00:22:25,567 --> 00:22:27,000
The best thing to do

522
00:22:27,133 --> 00:22:29,367
is follow Pops's instructions.

523
00:22:29,500 --> 00:22:33,267
Besides, we'll never know
when they'd make a move.

524
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:38,833
[OMENG] What is it?

525
00:22:38,967 --> 00:22:39,967
It's Gabo.

526
00:22:40,633 --> 00:22:42,333
Can we never mention
his name again?

527
00:22:43,433 --> 00:22:44,133
Every time we do,
he always pops up.

528
00:22:44,267 --> 00:22:46,733
Come on, get the gate.

529
00:22:46,867 --> 00:22:48,533
We'll let Pops know.

530
00:22:48,700 --> 00:22:49,667
Let's go.

531
00:22:50,033 --> 00:22:51,133
[METAL GATE SQUEAKS]

532
00:22:51,267 --> 00:22:54,400
[MOTORCYCLE REVVING]

533
00:22:54,533 --> 00:22:58,133
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

534
00:22:58,267 --> 00:23:00,667
Pops. Gabo is here.

535
00:23:01,267 --> 00:23:02,400
[GABO] Pops?

536
00:23:03,867 --> 00:23:04,833
[UWAK] Gabo?

537
00:23:05,167 --> 00:23:06,667
Didn't we tell you?

538
00:23:07,733 --> 00:23:09,167
We'll call you if we need you.
Why are you here?

539
00:23:09,300 --> 00:23:10,533
Where's Pops?

540
00:23:10,833 --> 00:23:11,600
I need a job.

541
00:23:11,733 --> 00:23:12,800
You're something else, Gabo.

542
00:23:13,667 --> 00:23:15,600
You've burned through
200,00 that quick?

543
00:23:18,133 --> 00:23:19,567
You know my situation.

544
00:23:20,433 --> 00:23:22,133
My father is in the hospital.

545
00:23:22,300 --> 00:23:23,500
I spent it on his surgery.

546
00:23:23,633 --> 00:23:25,500
Now, I need a job.

547
00:23:25,633 --> 00:23:27,600
We don't have any job for you.
Go home.

548
00:23:27,733 --> 00:23:29,800
And if we do,
we wouldn't give it to you.

549
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:32,100
You just got lucky
in the last one.

550
00:23:32,233 --> 00:23:34,000
You're pushing it now.

551
00:23:34,533 --> 00:23:35,500
I don't care
about either of you.

552
00:23:36,433 --> 00:23:38,800
You're not the one
I want to talk to.

553
00:23:39,700 --> 00:23:40,667
Pops!

554
00:23:41,267 --> 00:23:42,333
- Pops!
- [OMENG] Gabo.

555
00:23:43,033 --> 00:23:43,833
[GABO] Mister Omeng.

556
00:23:46,300 --> 00:23:47,333
Pops is waiting for you.

557
00:23:48,033 --> 00:23:49,133
This way.

558
00:23:49,567 --> 00:23:55,600
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

559
00:23:56,433 --> 00:23:57,300
I know.

560
00:23:57,433 --> 00:23:58,433
[CHUCKLES]

561
00:23:58,567 --> 00:24:00,633
I know what it'll take
for you to speak.

562
00:24:03,133 --> 00:24:04,967
- What is it?
- Django, what's this?

563
00:24:05,100 --> 00:24:06,233
- That's good!
- What's that?

564
00:24:06,367 --> 00:24:08,333
- Okay!
- What?

565
00:24:08,467 --> 00:24:11,400
- Time for a bath.
- Huh? But...

566
00:24:13,967 --> 00:24:15,100
Are you going to tell me now?

567
00:24:15,633 --> 00:24:17,233
Or do you want me
to dunk your heads in there?

568
00:24:17,367 --> 00:24:18,633
- No!
- No! Don't!

569
00:24:18,767 --> 00:24:19,967
Wait! Wait!

570
00:24:20,100 --> 00:24:21,900
We really don't know, Django.

571
00:24:22,033 --> 00:24:23,667
Actually, Gabo...

572
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:26,067
Gabo still doesn't
trust us fully.

573
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:27,667
He always turns us away.

574
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:29,300
He doesn't want us
to join his group.

575
00:24:29,467 --> 00:24:30,733
That's the truth.

576
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:34,067
- Oh!
- [DABOY] Stop!

577
00:24:34,367 --> 00:24:36,500
[MEN CACKLING]

578
00:24:36,633 --> 00:24:37,133
[BINOY] I don't know
how to swim!

579
00:24:37,267 --> 00:24:39,433
What?!

580
00:24:40,133 --> 00:24:40,567
[WHIMPERS]

581
00:24:40,700 --> 00:24:42,533
Wait! Wait!

582
00:24:42,667 --> 00:24:44,100
[COUGHS]

583
00:24:44,233 --> 00:24:47,167
[PANTS] Even if you kill us,

584
00:24:47,300 --> 00:24:48,333
you won't get anything from us.

585
00:24:48,467 --> 00:24:49,733
[TOLITS COUGHS]

586
00:24:50,300 --> 00:24:51,767
You know me, Tolits.

587
00:24:51,900 --> 00:24:53,533
I'm easy to talk to.

588
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:55,100
Kill them.

589
00:24:55,233 --> 00:24:56,867
- No! Stop!
- Wait!

590
00:24:57,000 --> 00:24:58,400
- No! No!
- No, please! No!

591
00:24:58,533 --> 00:24:59,300
- Wait! Wait! Wait!
- Django!

592
00:24:59,433 --> 00:25:02,100
I thought you'd dunk
our heads again.

593
00:25:02,267 --> 00:25:04,133
[CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY]
No. Don't kill us.

594
00:25:04,267 --> 00:25:05,867
[TOLITS] Wait. Hear me out.

595
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:08,067
The truth is,
we don't know anything.

596
00:25:08,433 --> 00:25:11,200
We haven't gained
Gabo's trust yet.

597
00:25:11,333 --> 00:25:14,333
But we can work on it.

598
00:25:14,467 --> 00:25:16,400
- What?!
- Here's what we're going to do.

599
00:25:18,233 --> 00:25:19,600
We'll try to befriend Gabo.

600
00:25:19,733 --> 00:25:21,133
And once we gain his trust,

601
00:25:21,267 --> 00:25:24,133
we can ask him what he does.

602
00:25:24,267 --> 00:25:27,433
And we can follow him
if you want us to.

603
00:25:27,567 --> 00:25:29,233
I thought Gabo
didn't trust you.

604
00:25:29,367 --> 00:25:30,500
For now.

605
00:25:30,633 --> 00:25:33,267
Right now, he doesn't trust us.

606
00:25:33,400 --> 00:25:35,467
But we're so close.

607
00:25:35,633 --> 00:25:37,333
So, Django, listen.

608
00:25:37,467 --> 00:25:39,100
If you let us go...

609
00:25:40,600 --> 00:25:43,900
we can spy on Gabo for you.

610
00:25:44,033 --> 00:25:50,900
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

611
00:25:52,700 --> 00:25:59,733
[MUSIC BECOMES STIRRING]

612
00:26:08,500 --> 00:26:09,600
Pops!

613
00:26:11,767 --> 00:26:13,633
I didn't ask you to come, Gabo.

614
00:26:14,433 --> 00:26:15,700
What do you need?

615
00:26:16,167 --> 00:26:17,333
Pops.

616
00:26:17,767 --> 00:26:21,000
I'm sorry for coming here again
unannounced.

617
00:26:22,033 --> 00:26:23,533
I need a job.

618
00:26:24,467 --> 00:26:26,033
I need money.

619
00:26:27,933 --> 00:26:29,967
I thought the time we
spent in prison

620
00:26:29,967 --> 00:26:32,100
was the hardest time
of my life.

621
00:26:32,100 --> 00:26:34,200
Because our lives
were in danger everyday.

622
00:26:34,200 --> 00:26:35,900
But thinking about it,

623
00:26:35,900 --> 00:26:37,533
we were more fortunate
back then

624
00:26:37,533 --> 00:26:39,533
because we had
a roof over our heads

625
00:26:39,533 --> 00:26:41,800
and our food was provided.

626
00:26:41,800 --> 00:26:43,500
But now that I've gotten out...

627
00:26:46,033 --> 00:26:48,400
I realized that life here
outside is much harder.

628
00:26:49,733 --> 00:26:52,333
Because you have
to fight every day

629
00:26:52,867 --> 00:26:54,267
just to live.

630
00:26:56,767 --> 00:26:58,567
Pops, I hope you'll hear
my request.

631
00:26:59,133 --> 00:27:01,300
I really need a job.

632
00:27:01,300 --> 00:27:02,300
[TOMAS] Pops.

633
00:27:02,700 --> 00:27:05,300
Gabo already proved
that we can count on him.

634
00:27:06,467 --> 00:27:08,367
He can help us out.

635
00:27:09,267 --> 00:27:11,267
I can give you a mission.

636
00:27:11,267 --> 00:27:13,633
But I don't know
if you're ready.

637
00:27:13,900 --> 00:27:16,567
Pops, Gabo is still new to this.

638
00:27:17,033 --> 00:27:18,767
He'll only end up in danger.

639
00:27:18,767 --> 00:27:20,100
A lot of people attempted
to do it,

640
00:27:20,100 --> 00:27:21,600
but they all failed.
And you expect him to succeed?

641
00:27:21,600 --> 00:27:23,700
Pops, he's right.

642
00:27:24,400 --> 00:27:26,467
Gabo won't be able
to handle this mission.

643
00:27:28,133 --> 00:27:29,800
What's your problem with me?

644
00:27:29,800 --> 00:27:31,800
I was able to accomplish
my last mission.

645
00:27:31,800 --> 00:27:33,100
You're saying that

646
00:27:33,467 --> 00:27:36,133
because you don't know
what's at stake.

647
00:27:36,133 --> 00:27:38,867
Uwak, let's give Gabo a chance.

648
00:27:40,700 --> 00:27:43,367
Pops, the decision is yours.

649
00:27:43,733 --> 00:27:50,700
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

650
00:27:50,867 --> 00:27:54,233
<i>During these times,
it's surprising to think</i>

651
00:27:54,233 --> 00:27:58,033
<i> that there are still people
who are willing to help</i>

652
00:27:58,033 --> 00:27:59,767
<i> without asking for anything
in exchange.</i>

653
00:27:59,767 --> 00:28:01,800
<i> His name is Gabo.</i>

654
00:28:01,800 --> 00:28:03,667
<i> This is the Zafras' fault!</i>

655
00:28:04,567 --> 00:28:06,067
<i> This case is hopeless now!</i>

656
00:28:06,067 --> 00:28:07,067
<i> Don't kill me!</i>

657
00:28:07,067 --> 00:28:08,100
<i> Mr. Chan!</i>

658
00:28:08,100 --> 00:28:09,333
<i> Don't kill me!</i>

659
00:28:09,333 --> 00:28:12,800
The only person who can help us
<i> solve this case</i>

660
00:28:12,800 --> 00:28:13,967
<i> is gone!</i>

661
00:28:13,967 --> 00:28:15,867
<i>I know that someone outside
is helping you.</i>

662
00:28:15,867 --> 00:28:18,233
<i>If I find out that
your parents are involved,</i>

663
00:28:18,233 --> 00:28:19,867
<i> you will be in jail together.</i>

664
00:28:19,867 --> 00:28:21,533
<i>Why don't you put
the long-haired guy in jail?</i>

665
00:28:21,533 --> 00:28:22,800
<i> You know him?</i>

666
00:28:22,833 --> 00:28:25,067
<i> One million pesos</i>

667
00:28:25,067 --> 00:28:27,300
every time you finish a mission.

668
00:28:27,300 --> 00:28:29,267
<i>That's a lot of money
for a mission.</i>

669
00:28:29,267 --> 00:28:32,267
<i>It just means that my life
will be at stake.</i>

670
00:28:32,267 --> 00:28:36,267
Once I'm out, I'll make you and
<i> the guy who put me here pay.</i>

671
00:28:36,267 --> 00:28:38,467
<i>This is all
Agent Jacinto's fault.</i>

672
00:28:38,467 --> 00:28:40,867
<i> I won't stop until I get even
with her.</i>

673
00:28:40,867 --> 00:28:42,300
<i> We need to put an end</i>

674
00:28:42,300 --> 00:28:43,900
<i> to all the bad guys out there.</i>

675
00:28:43,900 --> 00:28:45,167
<i> I accept your challenge.</i>

676
00:28:45,167 --> 00:28:47,133
<i> You have to become
an Anino.</i>
